      "ImageDescription": {
        "value": "Dogo Hot Spring main buildings seen from the mountain(KANMURI-YAMA)：This place was often described in Japanese literature, and it is said to be the oldest hot spring in Japan. Soseki Natsume, Shiki Masaoka and many other writers loved this place. The main wooden building built in 1894 was designated as the first national important cultural property as a public bath in 1994. (Ehime JAPAN)",
        "source": "commons-desc-page"
